From: Yanghan Ye <yyh94306@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] net: airoha: quarantine uncertain SOE SA slots

SOE completion descriptors carry only a slot index, not a generation.
Keep a retired index reserved until its old RCU completion readers have
left. A purged software context does not prove that its hardware packet
has drained, and failed staging/clear commits also leave uncertain state.

Remember when in-flight contexts were abandoned and quarantine slots
with uncertain programming, clearing or draining until provider reset.
Free their software state but do not let an old completion consume a new
SA's context. Normally drained and cleared slots remain reusable after
the grace period. The finite slot limit reports ENOSPC rather than
silently mixing stale cryptographic contexts after a hardware failure.

Signed-off-by: Yanghan Ye <yyh94306@gmail.com>
Assisted-by: Codex:GPT-5.6-sol
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_soe.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_soe.c
@@ -169,6 +169,7 @@
 	struct list_head rx_queue;
 	struct completion idle;
 	unsigned int inflight;
+	bool abandoned;
 	bool dead;
 };
 
@@ -635,6 +636,8 @@
 
 	err = airoha_soe_program_sa_locked(soe, i, &cfg);
 	if (err) {
+		/* A timed-out commit may still reach hardware; do not reuse its index. */
+		soe->sa_map |= BIT(i);
 		mutex_unlock(&soe->sa_lock);
 		kfree(new_sa);
 		return err;
@@ -707,6 +710,8 @@
 
 	spin_lock_bh(&sa->lock);
 	sa->dead = true;
+	if (sa->inflight)
+		sa->abandoned = true;
 	airoha_soe_forget_rx_ctx_list(sa);
 	list_splice_init(&sa->tx_queue, &tx_queue);
 	list_splice_init(&sa->rx_queue, &rx_queue);
@@ -723,13 +728,17 @@
 	LIST_HEAD(rx_queue);
 	LIST_HEAD(tx_queue);
 	struct airoha_soe *soe;
+	bool drained, release_slot = false;
+	int err;
 
 	if (!sa)
 		return;
 
 	soe = sa->soe;
 	airoha_soe_mark_sa_dead(sa);
-	if (!wait_for_completion_timeout(&sa->idle, AIROHA_SOE_SA_FREE_TIMEOUT))
+	drained = wait_for_completion_timeout(&sa->idle,
+					      AIROHA_SOE_SA_FREE_TIMEOUT);
+	if (!drained)
 		dev_warn(soe->dev,
 			 "timed out waiting for SOE SA%u in-flight packets\n",
 			 sa->index);
@@ -737,13 +746,23 @@
 	mutex_lock(&soe->sa_lock);
 	if (sa->index < AIROHA_SOE_NUM_SA &&
 	    rcu_access_pointer(soe->sa[sa->index]) == sa) {
-		airoha_soe_clear_sa_locked(soe, sa->index);
+		err = airoha_soe_clear_sa_locked(soe, sa->index);
 		RCU_INIT_POINTER(soe->sa[sa->index], NULL);
-		soe->sa_map &= ~BIT(sa->index);
+		release_slot = drained && !READ_ONCE(sa->abandoned) && !err;
+		if (!release_slot)
+			dev_warn(soe->dev, "quarantining SOE SA%u until reset\n",
+				 sa->index);
 	}
 	mutex_unlock(&soe->sa_lock);
 	synchronize_rcu();
 
+	/* Keep the index reserved until old completion readers have left. */
+	if (release_slot) {
+		mutex_lock(&soe->sa_lock);
+		soe->sa_map &= ~BIT(sa->index);
+		mutex_unlock(&soe->sa_lock);
+	}
+
 	spin_lock_bh(&sa->lock);
 	airoha_soe_forget_rx_ctx_list(sa);
 	list_splice_init(&sa->tx_queue, &tx_queue);
